request: Add a clear command that removes todos whose completed field is true.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, commands  (The request mentions a "completed" field, but Todo has no such field. The closest match is `done`, which the existing `complete` command sets, so I'm treating that as the field. The plan adds a `{kind:"clear"}` variant to Command in types. In commands it adds a pure clear() function, parseArgs support and run support, so the command is saved to disk.)
round 1: owners types=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 17/17 tests pass). The manifest now shows the Command union with a { kind: "clear" } variant and commands exporting clear(todos: Todo[]): Todo[]. Todo has no `completed` field, so the request's "completed field" was mapped to the existing `done` boolean. clear drops todos with done === true, parseArgs recognises `clear`, and run loads, clears, saves and reports how many were removed.)

